{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB13944 - MONDO_9047",
  "verbalization": "Testosterone Enanthate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Cryptorchidism (disease) through a series of interconnected pathways involving androgenic effects. The evidence suggests that Testosterone Enanthate may contribute to the development of Cryptorchidism via its role in inducing premature menopause or Klinefelter Syndrome, both of which are associated with reduced testicular function and hormonal imbalances. This is supported by the off-label use of Methyltestosterone and Fluoxymesterone, which are known to influence testicular development and hormone levels, ultimately leading to Cryptorchidism. The mechanisms underpinning this relationship are likely mediated through the disruption of normal testicular development and hormonal regulation, with Testosterone Enanthate acting as a precursor or modulator in this process. The evidence from the visible paths highlights a consistent link between Testosterone Enanthate and the disease, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
